text:
On September 15, 2026, Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) adopted a policy of removing the locations of thousands of individuals with final orders of removal from the Online Detainee Locator System (ODLS). This unprecedented policy change, designed to allow the swift deportation of noncitizens without access to counsel, the courts, or due process, has resulted in the United States government’s enforced disappearance of thousands of people in its custody.

The policy has obstructed legal counsel from accessing their clients in detention, preventing interventions to seek immigration relief, challenge unconstitutional detention, and block unlawful deportations. Families and community members are now unable to determine the location of their loved ones who are arrested and taken into ICE custody without notice.

What solutions exist?

The joint submission ask the Working Group on Enforced or Involuntary Disappearances (WGEID) to intervene by declaring that ICE’s new ODLS policy constitutes a policy of enforced disappearance and to take the following steps:

Issue a determination that ICE’s new ODLS policy constitutes a policy of enforced

disappearance;

Call on the United States government to end ICE’s new ODLS policy, immediately

restoring the access of noncitizens’ locations on the ODLS;

Call on the United States government to require DHS, including ICE and CBP, to publicly disclose a noncitizen’s location on the ODLS within one hour of their arrest or transfer;

Call on the United States government to require DHS, including ICE and CBP, to provide at least 24 hours notice to a noncitizen’s attorney of record prior to transferring that individual;

Publicly disclose any transmissions from the WGEID to the United States and any response by the United States government;

Conduct an urgent on-site mission to the United States to investigate the United States government’s implementation of the new ICE ODLS policy;

Hold a hearing during its winter or spring session of hearings on ICE’s new ODLS policy that results in the enforced disappearances of thousands of people with removal orders, as well as ongoing delays and deficiencies in the ODLS system that

result in enforced disappearances of people not covered by the policy.

How can I get involved?

